# SHA-256 of unchanged upstream imports: up:humanize @ 0.6.0 (self-authored).
#
# Upstream is this repository itself, not an external source. See the up:humanize
# entry in refactor/jstack-source-ledger.md (plugins/humanize/, self-authored).
# Therefore there is no LICENSE.* text here; byte binding and version provenance
# are the required records.
#
# Why frozen:
# tests/run_tests.py previously read upstream parity from the installation cache:
# ~/.claude/plugins/cache/<marketplace>/humanize/0.6.0/skills/humanize-kr/references
# That path disappears when plugins/humanize/ is deleted under the repack plan,
# versions advance beyond 0.6.0, or tests run on another machine. Its absence
# reduced four parity checks to one failure and broke check_total. It did not
# silently pass, but could only stay green on this machine.
#
# What is frozen:
# The check measures category IDs using ^#{2,3} ([A-Z]~?[A-Z]?-?\d*)\.
# Freeze whole originals anyway. Extracting only IDs risks later regenerating
# them from our own files and reducing the test to ours >= ours. Originals plus
# hashes preserve source provenance in the diff.
#
# Update procedure when upstream plugins/humanize/ advances beyond 0.6.0:
# 1. Copy the new version into tests/upstream-<version>/.
# 2. Update both hashes and directory names in this manifest.
# 3. Set run_tests.py UPSTREAM and UPSTREAM_PARITY floors from new measurements.
# 4. A reduced floor means upstream removed categories; record the evidence.
#
d80c55df7e207c47fe66d3359a98fcbd22ff1112330ac9512e0b44e00d2f4902  tests/upstream-0.6.0/ai-tell-taxonomy.md
554bda0e3dd1c754775c351baf8a78f9804b4f02cfba9982bd8d5fc3fac0e182  tests/upstream-0.6.0/procurement-taxonomy.md
